<p><em>The next hour, Mercer requested an interview with Dr. Dravis<br />
Dr. Dravis denied, stating that he would talk after Edward had</em></p>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Audio log entry-Interviewer-Dr. Mercer-Interviewee- Dr. Edward Date (𶐉𶐉𶐉𶐉𶐿𶐉)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- good evening Edward</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- good evening sir</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- would you please continue on the topic we’ve picked up last time</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- of course sir</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- please proceed then</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- well it was five days ago when the plant didn’t work as planned, actually it didn’t work at all, we checked the valves but it seemed that the methane was not enough, so three days later we-</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- would you please elaborate on the plant, and what it should have done?</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- oh, of course.<br />
(moment of silence)</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- please proceed.</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- well I’m trying to remember, the thing it was just, went so fast.</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- I understand.</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- Okay.</p>
<p>(moment of silence)</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- Alright, I got it.</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- Proceed</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- for a start sir we picked up traces of flora in the cave and knowing how caves form, we speculated that by now it would have been pent up with methane, potential energy, just sitting there waiting to be harvested, so that’s what we did, we harvested.</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>-I see, please continue</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- well sir three days later we checked on the cave personally, as Jacqe’s wish, we went down on a buggy in the cave we dug all those months ago, whilst wearing gas masks, heat resistant suits, oxygen tanks, sample vials, flashlights, an 800-foot rope ladder, Todd had a laser cutter in his forearm, and sir Dravis had a satchel, we wen-</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- what did the satchel contain?</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- oh, h-his journal sir, and a pen</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- oh, I see please continue</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>-we stopped at a dead end and went to the side of the tunnel, the tunnel had lights all over so we stayed our flashlights at the ready, Todd told us that we were at the top side of the cavity, he engaged his laser cutter, and started cutting a hole on the wall, and have pushed it, falling into an endless abyss,</p>
<p>If it were not for the light.</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>-light?</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>-(nods), it was such a beautiful sight, sir imagine expecting a half-assed shit hole only to see the oversight of a beautiful grass plain, the water-holes, the green grass, and a couple of forest patches, the light-brown walls covered with thousands of glimmering crystals just imagine heaven when we expected a shit-hole</p>
<p>(chuckles)</p>
<p>one can only imagine our emotions akin to those I'm sure of Columbus' sighting on the new world, as Jim managed to say under his breath “ exquisite, h-how?”. Todd said “fascinating, we need to study this”. Dravis with keen eyes, Saw a concrete facility just two klicks away, I grabbed my binoculars and confirmed Dravis’ claim, Jim requested that we camp there, we looked at Jim and Todd said, “good idea lets go now” before we could say anything Todd took some rope, tied it on the wall and went down enthusiastically, he motioned us to go down, Dravis and Jim followed enthusiastically, I hesitantly followed.</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- Hmmm I see, please continue.</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- When we got down, the ground was covered with grass, bushes, trees, individual water holes, and in the distance a forest, the walls were surprisingly smooth, they seemed to be man-made walls worn out with time, but probably not by man, a few moments later we spotted a river filled with fish, we were entranced by its beauty, that Jim managed to say “beautiful, just beautiful”, we walked towards the facility, Dravis, stopped, wrote a thing or two in his journal, then caught up.<br />
I couldn’t help but ask “sir Todd”, “yes” he replied, “did you know”, after a moment Todd replied “no, I might never have”, with that sir Todd went on, after a few moments later, the facility was now of sight,<br />
But something caught our eyes with awe once more.</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- what was it?</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- it was a cluster of crystals, which seemed to emit an almost blinding light, similar to that of the sun being covered by a light cluster of clouds, we looked away in doing so we realized that the same crystals had thrived on the roof above, dr. Dravis wrote in his journal this time a little longer.<br />
When we came to the facility’s door, we noticed an inscription on the side of the door, it seemed to be in German, we opened the door, but what we saw sir only strengthened the mystery</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- How so?</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- (shrugs), maybe but it certainly raised some alarms</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- I see, please continue</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- we opened the door and saw three Nazi skeletons aside a crate of rations, in the other side of the room a table filled with tools, syringes, wrenches, rusted microscopes, and two doors leading to rooms, as we opened the first room we saw that it had a broken glass window between the two rooms &quot;the observation room, or the testing chamber?&quot;, I thought, it was empty though and had bullet holes and claw marks, when we opened the other room, inside was a mess, broken tables chairs, heaps of ammunition were everywhere, some parts of the walls had bullet holes, but the thing that caught our attention was in the far corner</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- what was it?</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- it was a skeleton of a tiger or a lion but definitely of a cat’s, a cat the size of one and a half tigers, it had bullet holes in the cat’s head, spine, and limbs, two or four ribs were shattered, but some of the bullet holes showed rapid healing as we saw some of the bullets were pushed from the bone, its head was something out from a horror film, the skull had two canines protruding from the lower jaw like that of a wild boar, its lower jaw was the size of its skull, it had a casing underneath, similar to that of its cranium, and if it were the skull it lacked a nasal cavity, and eye sockets, we opened the mandible a few minutes later and discovered that it was hollow, with its contents dried out, containing God knows what</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- I see, what else did you see in the room?</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- well, we saw a Nazi soldier’s skeleton ripped in half, near his hand a rifle, the other skeleton was a Nazi scientist holding a journal with its ribs and spine shattered, the journal however German we still saw several illustrations and diagrams of skeletons of animals with the same distinct mandible, other illustrations show these animals with skin and had four ears, two on the top and two on the bottom.</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- how did you determine those skeletons to be Nazis?</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- uhm, their armbands sir</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- I see, you may please continue to what happened next</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- well sir we radioed jacqe about everything we found, he had a contemptuous voice at first, but slowly as we explained he slowly became more and more professional, he spoke, well, well he spoke a lot like you, sir, with all those “I SEE’s” of his.</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- I-, (moment of silence), please continue</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- we asked him to bring supplies and additional equipment, that we may camp here</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- I guess that’s not what came?</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- I and sir Dravis owe you for that, we didn’t quite think that armed men would be more useful than a couple of errand boys.<br />
(moment of silence)</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- so Edward, what happened after that?</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>- after we radioed jacqe, we head outside to gather samples of the crystals, dirt, plants and the walls, we caught a few rabbits and we all went towards the water hole, for we realized that we were a group too small and too inexperienced to separate,<br />
t-the, the</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- then were you attacked or was it something else?</p>
<p><strong>Edward</strong>-(nods), ye-yes sir, we were attacked</p>
<p><strong>Mercer</strong>- may we please continue</p>
