<p><strong>Audio log entry Interviewer- Madam Schnouze Interviewee- Dr. Todd, date(𶐉𶐉𶐉𶐉𶐿𶐉)</strong></p>
<p><strong>Madam Schnouze</strong>- Dr. Todd, good afternoon</p>
<p><strong>Todd</strong>- good afternoon to you too Schnouze, now we’ve talked with Dravis and we have decided that I would best deliver the message, the journal, and the questions you ask</p>
<p><strong>Madam Schnouze</strong>- Dr. Todd, have you deciphered the writings on the walls?</p>
<p><strong>Todd</strong>-Yes, it was hard and long but we managed</p>
<p><strong>Madam Schnouze</strong>- what did it say?</p>
<p><strong>Todd</strong>- a lot actually in this journal (hands journal), it was an ancient memoir, shorn of fable, reviving a man, not an unnatural puff of heaven, Incredible yet credible</p>
<p><strong>Madam Schnouze</strong>- to whom?</p>
<p><strong>Todd</strong>- in the memory of the children of the night</p>
<p><strong>Madam Schnouze</strong>- SCP 1000?</p>
<p><strong>Todd</strong>- indeed so</p>
<p><strong>Madam Schnouze</strong>- what else would you like to say</p>
<p><strong>Todd</strong>- and as I quote on the last part of the inscription, which said as I remember, “The children of the sun had reduced our glimmering cities to ash, the day of the flowers is nigh, and may this vault safeguard our knowledge”, deliver this journal to the 05-council they’ll know what to do</p>
<p><strong>Madam Schnouze</strong>- as you wish, (opens the book on a random page), (glares at page), the Tarasque?</p>
<p><strong>Todd</strong>- no Madam Schnouze, I believe it's famine.</p>
<p><strong>End audio log</strong></p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<blockquote>
<p><strong>audio log-Madam Schnouze</strong></p>
<p>I have read the journal, and the staff at the site specifically Todd and his associates directed a hypothesis that in speculation that the scarlet king had the horsemen(the umber is inconsistent), and the horsemen could never die, as they are spirits that possess another body after their own would perish by pure chance after death, after possession, during this period they will retain the memories of the possessed due to a curse by (redacted) but after a series of mental interaction with surviving horsemen, they will retain their apocalyptical goals no matter how specialized their possessed memories' philosophy can be therefore their goal can never be stopped, only extended, with this they enhance the host's capabilities to an extent that causes havoc,</p>
<p>We have contained at least three of the theorized horsemen, namely famine, war, and death, death has been theorized to possess a body of a female child designated as <a class="newpage" href="/scp-53">SCP 53</a>, famine, as <a href="/scp-682">SCP 682</a>, with war possessing that of <a href="/scp-4715">SCP-4715</a> even if this is mere speculation, we need to act and place wagers, bet that the four horsemen are true and are needed to be immobilized and not to terminate,</p>
<p>if we gain, we gain humanity's security, if this speculation is nothing but mere speculation, then we lose nothing, so, therefore, the action is needed</p>
</blockquote>
